# Build the delivery-bar steering prose and morning digest

From [Decide the Telegram delivery bar](./decide-telegram-delivery-bar.svx):
the gateway delivers ~66 Telegram messages/day against an approved ~13. The
bar is settled; this step lands it in the gateway's steering prose and gives
the demoted traffic somewhere to go.

Resolved when:

- `roles/gateway.md` carries the bar: a ping means waiting-on-Joel-and-aging,
  important first-notice breakage, or an answer to what he asked. One incident
  = one thread until it closes. Worker DONE receipts never ping individually.
  Producer runbook cadence is evidence, not instruction. "Ack Before Working"
  is scoped to addressed inbound only.
- Digest guidance is written as intent, not spec (Joel: inference over
  specification): morning digest leads with "waiting on you" ranked by age ×
  importance, composed from live state at send time, context/thread/project
  aware by the agent's own judgment. One standalone ping per threshold
  crossing; digest carries it thereafter unless something material changes.
- A ~07:30 beat wakes the gateway to compose the digest — ride the existing
  pane-schedule/wake path; the digest is judgment, so it lands in the gateway
  queue, not a beat lane.

